# Project: Model

Purpose:
  Define how the real software project is represented inside the SDD
  project model. This file is the thin index — focused modules own
  the actual content.

Modules:
  schema:       @schema.sdd        (core hierarchy: Project > Domain > Module > Feature > Component)
  profile:      @profile.sdd       (project operational context: stack, scale, availability, compliance)
  ownership:    @ownership.sdd     (ownership rules for project elements)
  code-mapping: @code-mapping.sdd  (source code to semantic identifier mapping)
  drift:        @drift.sdd         (declared/observed/drift model, graph drift, fallback discovery)
  decisions:    @decisions.sdd     (project decision storage, indexing, retrieval, impact workflow)
  docs:         @docs.sdd          (human-readable documentation structure and metadata)
  risk:         @risk.sdd          (risk register schema)

Siblings:
  domains:      @domains.sdd       (domain schema and concrete domain list)
  modules:      @modules.sdd       (module schema and concrete module list)
  map:          @map.sdd           (project navigation map)
  dependencies: @dependencies.sdd  (concrete dependency graph)
  indexes:      @indexes.sdd       (category-level fast navigation index)
  architecture: @architecture.sdd  (project concrete architecture)
  flows:        @flows.sdd         (project execution flow)
  instantiation:@instantiation.sdd (how a project instance gets decided)

Rules:
  [PM1] Every project domain MUST have a model file (bax ./domains.sdd).
  [PM2] Every domain SHOULD expose its boundaries and declare owned components.
  [PM3] Project elements MUST NOT duplicate information owned by global SDD systems — reference them instead.
  [PM4] Feature declarations MUST reference the chain type they run under (bax chains/chains.sdd).
  [PM5] Feature/component declarations MUST reference task and decision rules.
  [PM6] Component code paths MUST be mapped to project ownership.
  [PM7] AI SHOULD use this project model to locate code before searching the source tree.
  [PM8] This file MUST NOT redeclare concrete domain/module lists already owned by domains.sdd/modules.sdd.
  [PM9] Populating hierarchy layers beyond what current analysis justifies is FORBIDDEN (bax ./instantiation.sdd).
  [PM10] Every project element MUST have one clear owner.

Portability:
  This file MUST remain reusable across projects unchanged — it defines
  the SHAPE of the hierarchy. Concrete instances belong to sibling files.

State: +
